    "updated_at": "2023-08-23T22:31:25Z",
    "body": "> As far as I can tell, these init structs are \"kind of?\" non-normative.\r\n\r\nWithout these, it would be impossible to do `new PopStateEvent(\"popstate\", { hasUAVisualTransition: true })`. We want that sort of thing to be possible for all events, in order to make testing and mocking easier.\r\n\r\n@khushalsagar can you write a test for such synthetic events? E.g. https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/navigation-api/navigate-event/event-constructor.html should be updated for `NavigateEvent`; I'm not sure if a similar test exists for `PopStateEvent`.\r\n\r\n(Or @ADKaster, let us know if you want to work on the tests instead!)",
